# The shipped top-level entry set — ONE source of truth (S2, 0.12).
#
# Every entry point that stages a Hive copy reads this list:
#   - packaging/build-package.sh stages these entries into the tarball
#     and writes them into MANIFEST.txt (S1)
#   - packaging/install.sh --copy-to stages the SAME set into the
#     install dir
#
# Nothing outside the set is ever staged: runtime state (.company/,
# .worktrees/), build artifacts (dist/), and local junk cannot reach a
# tarball or an install, and unreadable or unexpected paths elsewhere
# in the source cannot abort a copy (the rsync exit 23 hard-fail).
#
# Format (parsed by packaging/entries.sh):
#   one entry per line; comments (#) and blank lines are ignored.
#   A one-field line names an entry that exists at the source root —
#   a directory or a file, staged under its own name.
#   "SRC as DEST" stages SRC under the name DEST (the public README.md
#   ships from share/docs/README.md).
bin
lib
etc
share
packaging
VERSION
share/docs/README.md as README.md
INSTALL
LICENSE
CHANGELOG.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
SECURITY.md
# T3 (0.13): the shipping manifest ships to the install (doctor's
# installed-set check reads it there). The build generates it — from
# a git checkout it is absent and staged as a NOTE-free skip.
MANIFEST.txt
